1
00:00:01,868 --> 00:00:05,505
<i>Hilar bile duct cancer. Stage 3.</i>

2
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:06,773
You have six months to live.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:08,375
Daimon, you do the surgery.

4
00:00:09,242 --> 00:00:10,243
I'm counting on you.

5
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:14,481
The donor of the liver
for this surgery is his wife.

6
00:00:14,547 --> 00:00:19,219
The primary surgeon
is Professor Ikuya Hijikata.

7
00:00:19,285 --> 00:00:20,453
Let's begin.

8
00:00:21,254 --> 00:00:23,556
You there. Get out of my way.
He's my patient.

9
00:00:23,623 --> 00:00:25,592
Get out of the operating room
this instant!

10
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:28,061
- No way.
- It's signed by Professor Torii

11
00:00:28,128 --> 00:00:29,396
when he was still conscious.

12
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:33,099
Why did Professor Torii
choose you to be his primary surgeon?

13
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:37,470
- Because I will not fail.
- Michiko Daimon.

14
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:48,848
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

15
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:51,451
LIVING DONOR LIVER TRANSPLANT

16
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:52,919
- Metzen.
- Yes.

17
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:57,891
Anastomosis of liver graft

18
00:00:57,957 --> 00:01:00,427
and recipient's hepatic vein,
portal vein complete.

19
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:02,762
- Resume blood flow.
- Yes.

20
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,635
We got blood flowing in the graft now.

21
00:01:08,701 --> 00:01:09,536
HIDEKI KAJI

22
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:11,438
MAMORU HARA

23
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,572
HIKARU MORIMOTO

24
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:13,573
All right.

25
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,241
ANESTHESIOLOGIST
HIROMI JONOUCHI

26
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:18,545
Next, we'll start
with anastomosis of the hepatic vein.

27
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:20,447
- Microscope.
- Yes.

28
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:21,781
- Take off the loupe.
- Yes.

29
00:01:28,488 --> 00:01:29,956
- 8-0 nylon.
- Yes.

30
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:32,959
- Micro forceps.
- Yes.

31
00:01:33,026 --> 00:01:34,294
- Saline, please.
- Yes.

32
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:37,864
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA

33
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:39,866
AKIRA KANBARA

34
00:01:54,514 --> 00:01:57,884
Professor Busujima.
Is the surgery going well?

35
00:01:58,351 --> 00:02:02,922
- Chairman Teshigawara.
- How do you do, sir?

36
00:02:03,056 --> 00:02:04,891
TSUYOSHI TESHIGAWARA

37
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,430
Why isn't Hijikata performing the surgery?

38
00:02:12,031 --> 00:02:13,600
Who is that woman?

39
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:18,171
Yes. Well, she's... She's...

40
00:02:18,838 --> 00:02:21,841
Why, if it isn't the honorable
Mr. Chairman from the main hospital.

41
00:02:22,108 --> 00:02:25,111
That woman is Michiko Daimon
from our referral agency.

42
00:02:25,578 --> 00:02:26,513
Referral agency?

43
00:02:31,284 --> 00:02:32,385
Professor Busujima.

44
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:34,954
What's going on?

45
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:52,705
Blood pressure, top has dropped to 70.

46
00:02:55,074 --> 00:02:57,110
- What's bleeding?
- Why?

47
00:02:57,177 --> 00:02:58,411
This isn't good.

48
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,547
- Morimoto, take over suction.
- Yes.

49
00:03:00,813 --> 00:03:04,117
Heavy bleeding from the graft.
I can't suture in this condition.

50
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,318
What do we do?

51
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,587
We'll look for the source of bleeding.

52
00:03:07,787 --> 00:03:08,788
- Mosquito.
- Yes.

53
00:03:13,326 --> 00:03:15,495
Bleeding from the graft?

54
00:03:15,562 --> 00:03:17,197
- Damn.
- Will he be all right?

55
00:03:17,263 --> 00:03:18,097
KANEKO TERAYAMA

56
00:03:18,965 --> 00:03:21,167
What will happen to the Master Award?

57
00:03:21,968 --> 00:03:23,336
What's happening? What's going on?

58
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:24,804
PROFESSOR TAKASHI TORII

59
00:03:30,109 --> 00:03:33,713
If you let him bleed to death here,

60
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,115
you're finished.

61
00:03:38,084 --> 00:03:39,152
I'm aware of that.

62
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:45,725
Sir? Director,
where are you going? Director!

63
00:03:50,496 --> 00:03:55,435
Blood pressure, top is below 60 now.
Heart rate 140. MAP 20 units, stat.

64
00:03:55,501 --> 00:03:56,469
Got it.

65
00:03:57,604 --> 00:04:01,341
The only thing I can think of
is artery dissection in the graft.

66
00:04:02,275 --> 00:04:04,844
What do we do? We can't backtrack now.

67
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:06,980
Where the heck is it bleeding from?

68
00:04:15,989 --> 00:04:17,123
Director Busujima.

69
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:23,796
Daimon. That's why I told you!

70
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:26,332
You should've let Hijikata do it!

71
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,168
Move. I'll do it myself.

72
00:04:29,869 --> 00:04:31,237
We're stopping the heart.

73
00:04:32,138 --> 00:04:33,039
What?

74
00:04:33,806 --> 00:04:35,174
The heart?

75
00:04:36,075 --> 00:04:37,777
No way. Has she gone insane?

76
00:04:38,244 --> 00:04:42,382
Someone, stop Ms. Daimon!
Make her stop! Hey!

77
00:04:43,016 --> 00:04:44,417
Stop the heart?

78
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:47,220
We'll stop the heart temporarily,
stop the bleeding,

79
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:50,089
identify the dissection,
and restore it. Administer ATP.

80
00:04:50,156 --> 00:04:52,925
That's impossible. Time limit is
a minute and a half at the most.

81
00:04:52,992 --> 00:04:54,861
- It's too risky.
- Are you serious?

82
00:04:54,927 --> 00:04:57,363
That's more than enough time.
Hurry up and stop it.

83
00:05:04,103 --> 00:05:06,572
- Administering ATP. Get it ready.
- Yes.

84
00:05:36,369 --> 00:05:37,303
Kaji.

85
00:05:45,244 --> 00:05:47,013
Open up this part with a Pean
so I can see.

86
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,481
- Pean.
- Yes.

87
00:05:55,488 --> 00:05:57,724
Show me the tip
of this blood vessel with a Kelly.

88
00:05:57,790 --> 00:05:59,726
- Fine-tipped Kelly.
- Yes.

89
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:15,007
Director. Director!

90
00:06:15,074 --> 00:06:19,011
Please! Don't kill him!

91
00:06:28,654 --> 00:06:30,223
- Found it.
- Here it is.

92
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:31,891
- 8-0 nylon.
- Yes.

93
00:06:31,958 --> 00:06:35,194
- Heart beat resuming in 20 seconds.
- Crap, that's not enough time.

94
00:06:45,438 --> 00:06:46,272
So fast.

95
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:05,258
Repair of dissection complete.

96
00:07:08,561 --> 00:07:12,632
Heartbeat resumed.
Hemodynamics, all normal.

97
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,837
- We did it.
- Director, excuse me.

98
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:30,483
- Made it in time.
- That took a few years off my life.

99
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:37,223
Once again,
begin anastomosis of hepatic vein.

100
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:38,925
- One more 8-0.
- Yes.

101
00:07:41,394 --> 00:07:43,663
- Director, I'll take your place.
- Yes.

102
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:44,764
- Forceps.
- Yes.

103
00:07:44,864 --> 00:07:46,032
Beginning suction.

104
00:08:09,856 --> 00:08:10,957
That woman...

105
00:08:11,424 --> 00:08:14,594
Like I said,
she's Michiko Daimon from our agency.

106
00:08:28,941 --> 00:08:29,909
Ladies and gentlemen...

107
00:08:31,143 --> 00:08:34,347
please forget what you saw here.

108
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:39,485
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir!

109
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:44,457
I've made reservations
at a steak house after this.

110
00:08:44,924 --> 00:08:46,292
That's a wonderful idea.

111
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:50,196
The surgery went on for nine hours,
everyone must be hungry. Please go.

112
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:54,367
Go enjoy the delicious steak
with Professor Teshigawara. Come now!

113
00:08:54,433 --> 00:08:58,271
Thank you for your hard work.
Please watch your step. Thank you!

114
00:09:10,016 --> 00:09:13,419
Professor Torii's surgery
ended successfully.

115
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,254
We're all relieved.

116
00:09:15,321 --> 00:09:16,689
PROFESSOR TORII'S WIFE
NANAKO TORII

117
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:18,891
CHIEF NURSE
SONOKO CHIBA

118
00:09:18,958 --> 00:09:20,393
Professor fought hard in there.

119
00:09:21,827 --> 00:09:23,596
I would hope so.

120
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:30,436
I won't let him get away if he died
after making me give up my liver.

121
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:49,021
Are you Daimon?

122
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,565
Do you like steak?

123
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,402
- Yes, very much.
- Medium?

124
00:10:04,203 --> 00:10:05,338
Rare?

125
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:09,008
I'm inviting you along with the press.

126
00:10:10,743 --> 00:10:12,478
I don't know who you are, but...

127
00:10:13,546 --> 00:10:14,547
I'm not doing it.

128
00:10:21,887 --> 00:10:24,156
Not doing it, huh?

129
00:10:36,335 --> 00:10:38,771
I watched from a monitor in another room.

130
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:44,210
- It was a brilliant surgery.
- How about apologizing first?

131
00:10:44,276 --> 00:10:46,712
It's your fault we had to stop the heart.

132
00:10:46,779 --> 00:10:50,249
Artery dissection in the donor's liver
is an unpredictable condition.

133
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:52,251
If I was performing the surgery...

134
00:10:52,318 --> 00:10:53,185
IKUYA HIJIKATA

135
00:10:53,252 --> 00:10:54,987
...I could've repaired it immediately.

136
00:10:56,989 --> 00:11:01,694
Professors never admit
their mistakes, do they?

137
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:06,832
I talked Director Busujima
into retracting your termination.

138
00:11:09,201 --> 00:11:11,303
You worked hard
through a nine-hour surgery.

139
00:11:12,271 --> 00:11:13,406
I bet you're hungry, huh?

140
00:11:13,806 --> 00:11:15,574
I made reservations at that restaurant.

141
00:11:15,641 --> 00:11:16,676
I'm not doing it.

142
00:11:20,946 --> 00:11:21,881
I see.

143
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,250
Well...

144
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:26,052
take care.

145
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,255
Mr. Hijikata?

146
00:11:31,557 --> 00:11:34,393
Please be a professor
who never makes mistakes.

147
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:36,529
Goodbye.

148
00:11:40,066 --> 00:11:43,502
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

149
00:11:45,638 --> 00:11:48,340
<i>University hospital</i>
<i>medical offices were losing power,</i>

150
00:11:49,108 --> 00:11:51,143
<i>and even medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with life and death,</i>

151
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:54,580
<i>plunged into an era</i>
<i>where the law of the jungle prevailed.</i>

152
00:12:00,352 --> 00:12:01,320
How is he doing?

153
00:12:01,921 --> 00:12:05,291
- Yes. He's in stable condition.
- Good.

154
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:09,595
Regarding the surgery today,

155
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:14,033
keep in mind that Professor Hijikata
did it as originally planned.

156
00:12:18,471 --> 00:12:19,538
Do you understand?

157
00:12:24,043 --> 00:12:28,280
<i>To fill the critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field are the freelance.</i>

158
00:12:29,482 --> 00:12:32,685
<i>In other words, a lone wolf doctor.</i>

159
00:12:34,153 --> 00:12:36,455
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

160
00:12:38,891 --> 00:12:43,662
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

161
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:48,667
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

162
00:12:55,241 --> 00:12:56,976
Hi, Michiko. You worked hard.

163
00:12:58,043 --> 00:13:00,546
Congratulations on your first
living donor liver transplant.

164
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:01,580
Thank you.

165
00:13:09,054 --> 00:13:11,657
You've improved your skill again.

166
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:13,626
Really?

167
00:13:13,993 --> 00:13:16,495
You even fixed
Professor Hijikata's screwup today.

168
00:13:16,562 --> 00:13:19,331
Well done. That's my disciple.

169
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:22,935
All right. My master gave me a compliment.

170
00:13:23,736 --> 00:13:26,038
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

171
00:13:27,072 --> 00:13:28,140
<i>Also known as...</i>

172
00:13:29,041 --> 00:13:30,576
<i>Doctor X.</i>

173
00:13:38,884 --> 00:13:41,787
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 8

174
00:13:44,523 --> 00:13:47,993
Professor Torii, congratulations
on your successful surgery.

175
00:13:48,127 --> 00:13:49,028
Thank you.

176
00:13:49,395 --> 00:13:51,897
GOT, GPT, bilirubin,
and other liver functions,

177
00:13:51,964 --> 00:13:56,001
white blood cell count, and other
inflammatory reactions, are all improving.

178
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,804
And your wife is
recovering very nicely as well.

179
00:13:58,871 --> 00:13:59,939
I see.

180
00:14:00,472 --> 00:14:02,074
You can close your top now.

181
00:14:05,144 --> 00:14:07,479
Daimon, thank you.

182
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:11,150
Your surgery scar is really clean indeed.

183
00:14:11,951 --> 00:14:14,687
Unlike you, I have skill.

184
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:16,956
Daimon. Watch your mouth.

185
00:14:21,794 --> 00:14:23,195
I read the article on Hijikata.

186
00:14:23,262 --> 00:14:24,296
HIJIKATA, PRIMARY SURGEON

187
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:28,100
Frankly, I was surprised that my wife
agreed to donate her liver to me,

188
00:14:28,634 --> 00:14:30,603
but after I read this, it became clear.

189
00:14:30,669 --> 00:14:34,840
Director Busujima must've
talked her into it for hospital politics,

190
00:14:35,774 --> 00:14:37,243
and she probably couldn't refuse.

191
00:14:38,344 --> 00:14:39,278
Are you stupid?

192
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:42,548
- Daimon.
- Hospital politics?

193
00:14:44,850 --> 00:14:47,386
Do you really think
she went through all that pain,

194
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:50,723
to donate her healthy liver
for a stupid reason like that?

195
00:14:51,657 --> 00:14:55,694
I'm really sorry.
This idiot doesn't know how to talk.

196
00:14:55,761 --> 00:14:56,996
If I may translate,

197
00:14:57,096 --> 00:15:00,633
I think she wanted to say
that your wife loves you very much.

198
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:03,269
Hey, let's get going.

199
00:15:04,336 --> 00:15:05,304
Let's go.

200
00:15:05,938 --> 00:15:07,106
Excuse me.

201
00:15:12,945 --> 00:15:14,780
- I'm fine. I can walk now.
- Yes.

202
00:15:21,487 --> 00:15:22,621
Dr. Daimon,

203
00:15:23,789 --> 00:15:27,426
thank you for saving my husband's life.

204
00:15:38,804 --> 00:15:40,472
You look better than I expected.

205
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:42,908
Is your surgical wound healing all right?

206
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:48,847
My scar doesn't look too clean.

207
00:15:49,315 --> 00:15:52,351
That's because Hijikata did yours.

208
00:15:55,587 --> 00:16:00,859
I also have this other jagged scar
from your appendectomy years ago.

209
00:16:02,761 --> 00:16:04,663
I can't catch a break.

210
00:16:16,241 --> 00:16:18,510
This is terrible! This is disastrous!

211
00:16:25,617 --> 00:16:31,190
Director! Oh, my God! Take a look at this!

212
00:16:35,294 --> 00:16:37,096
COLLAPSE OF THE IVORY TOWER

213
00:16:41,633 --> 00:16:43,302
FREELANCE SURGEON

214
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,138
SINISTER WOMAN DOCTOR

215
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,244
"Collapse of the Ivory Tower"?

216
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:56,615
"Freelance surgeon operates on
Master Award candidate, Professor Torii."

217
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,751
Won't this get us in trouble?

218
00:16:58,817 --> 00:17:00,753
"Who is this sinister woman doctor?"

219
00:17:10,062 --> 00:17:11,997
Have you had the chance to read that yet?

220
00:17:16,835 --> 00:17:17,870
This is who I am.

221
00:17:20,139 --> 00:17:21,540
<i>Weekly Real?</i>

222
00:17:24,309 --> 00:17:26,211
Does that mean you wrote this article?

223
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:29,148
That's Part 1.

224
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:30,649
JOURNALIST
RYO YAGI

225
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:34,053
Part 2 is how did
such an outrageous thing happen?

226
00:17:35,154 --> 00:17:39,591
I plan to delve deeply into
rotten politics at university hospitals.

227
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:42,061
Wait a minute, please.

228
00:17:42,127 --> 00:17:45,164
Let's talk it over. Okay? Let's talk.

229
00:17:46,298 --> 00:17:47,266
Now, then.

230
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,868
Director Busujima.

231
00:18:06,518 --> 00:18:08,520
"Who is this sinister woman doctor?

232
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:13,058
There were also doctors
and patients who claim she's Doctor X."

233
00:18:13,125 --> 00:18:15,294
- Oh, dear.
- Doctor X?

234
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:19,765
That Doctor X who performs
shady surgeries for money is Michiko?

235
00:18:19,865 --> 00:18:20,866
No way.

236
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:24,436
Tabloid magazines sure write
a bunch of lies.

237
00:18:24,903 --> 00:18:28,006
How can Michiko be Doctor X?

238
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,842
Because...

239
00:18:32,377 --> 00:18:33,479
Because what?

240
00:18:33,712 --> 00:18:36,415
Nothing. This article is really terrible.

241
00:18:36,482 --> 00:18:37,483
Throw it away.

242
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:40,719
I'm not staying here.
I'm changing hospitals.

243
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,021
What'll happen if I get operated on
by this sinister doctor?

244
00:18:43,088 --> 00:18:45,991
I'm canceling tomorrow's surgery!

245
00:18:46,091 --> 00:18:47,159
Please reconsider.

246
00:18:47,226 --> 00:18:49,228
Sir! You have a fever, don't you?

247
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:51,763
- Let's get you treated at once!
- Please wait, sir. Please.

248
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:54,700
Sir, we'll get you in right away!

249
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,736
Mom, let's go elsewhere.
This place can't be trusted.

250
00:19:03,675 --> 00:19:05,878
You guys look bored.

251
00:19:07,546 --> 00:19:10,983
Just today, three surgeries were canceled.

252
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:14,720
A flood of appointment cancellations.
The hospital's reputation hit rock bottom.

253
00:19:14,786 --> 00:19:17,122
Office manager was crying
that the hospital's going under.

254
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:20,325
It's as if we're criminals.

255
00:19:21,627 --> 00:19:25,864
"Members of the medical staff
who supported the sinister doctor."

256
00:19:26,865 --> 00:19:30,936
So? Where did this sinister doctor go?

257
00:19:32,137 --> 00:19:34,273
Come to think of it,
I haven't seen her all morning.

258
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,707
She probably escaped somewhere.

259
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:39,711
- Escape?
- I thought she was devious,

260
00:19:39,778 --> 00:19:41,480
but who would've thought she was Doctor X?

261
00:19:45,584 --> 00:19:47,452
Pelvic exenteration surgery is done.

262
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:49,721
It sure is tiring to be
on your feet eight hours straight.

263
00:19:49,788 --> 00:19:51,056
Man, I'm starving.

264
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:53,725
This isn't the time to be starving.

265
00:19:53,926 --> 00:19:56,028
So, you were operating,
unaware of any of this?

266
00:19:57,095 --> 00:19:58,931
What's the matter? Did something happen?

267
00:19:58,997 --> 00:20:01,266
- Your picture is in it, too.
- What?

268
00:20:01,333 --> 00:20:04,803
Demon, look. You got your face shown.

269
00:20:05,904 --> 00:20:08,440
- We could be in trouble!
- That's right.

270
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:11,443
Thanks to the sinister doctor,
we're in trouble, too.

271
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:12,878
Hey, say something.

272
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:14,646
What's this? I can't forgive this.

273
00:20:15,113 --> 00:20:19,418
I look so bad. I'm not looking
at the camera, and look scary.

274
00:20:20,118 --> 00:20:21,086
Give me a break.

275
00:20:23,455 --> 00:20:24,423
That's your concern?

276
00:20:28,293 --> 00:20:30,329
- Excuse me.
- Excuse me!

277
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,531
The doctor who operated
on Professor Torii's here, right?

278
00:20:32,598 --> 00:20:34,733
This is <i>Weekly Woman.</i>
Please let us interview her!

279
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,001
Sinister Doctor!

280
00:20:36,501 --> 00:20:39,304
Excuse me.
Is the content of the article true?

281
00:20:39,938 --> 00:20:43,575
- They're so noisy.
- The hospital called.

282
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:46,778
You're ordered to stay home
until things settle down.

283
00:20:47,479 --> 00:20:52,017
Damn. Whoever wrote that article
was at surgery, right?

284
00:20:52,684 --> 00:20:55,554
That person even knew
that the heart was stopped during surgery.

285
00:20:55,621 --> 00:20:57,189
Any suspicions in the observation room?

286
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,724
There was someone black-hearted.

287
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:02,160
Chairman at the main hospital,
Tsuyoshi Teshigawara.

288
00:21:02,227 --> 00:21:03,161
Teshigawara?

289
00:21:03,795 --> 00:21:07,232
<i>To begin with, Busujima,</i>
<i>who was aiming for the Director's seat</i>

290
00:21:07,299 --> 00:21:09,601
<i>at the main hospital,</i>
<i>was demoted to the 3rd hospital</i>

291
00:21:09,668 --> 00:21:13,071
<i>because Teshigawara</i>
<i>leaked dirt on him to the management.</i>

292
00:21:13,138 --> 00:21:17,342
After leaking and pulling each other down,
Teshigawara persevered.

293
00:21:17,409 --> 00:21:21,747
Meaning he's ten times
more black-hearted than Busujima.

294
00:21:21,813 --> 00:21:23,749
That would be pitch black.

295
00:21:26,018 --> 00:21:27,953
Is Doctor X in there?

296
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,756
Of course not. Right, Michiko?

297
00:21:31,523 --> 00:21:33,292
<i>Ron. Riichi,</i> only.

298
00:21:34,026 --> 00:21:36,094
So do I.

299
00:21:39,398 --> 00:21:40,365
Sinister doctor!

300
00:21:40,432 --> 00:21:41,633
We know you're in there.

301
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,502
- Sinister doctor!
- Hey, sinister!

302
00:21:43,568 --> 00:21:44,770
I'm not sinister!

303
00:21:49,408 --> 00:21:54,112
Well, that was
a pretty interesting article.

304
00:21:55,047 --> 00:21:56,248
Thank you very much.

305
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,589
Write some more.

306
00:22:11,396 --> 00:22:12,497
Leave it to me.

307
00:22:13,865 --> 00:22:16,134
I'm working on Part 2 and Part 3.

308
00:22:18,303 --> 00:22:19,871
It's a minor story, but...

309
00:22:19,938 --> 00:22:23,675
I have material on Professor Torii
and his mistress, too.

310
00:22:28,914 --> 00:22:32,884
- I'll have another glass of Opus.
- Yes, sir.

311
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:39,658
The Third Hospital is
in serious trouble, isn't it?

312
00:22:40,058 --> 00:22:44,529
Professor Busujima,
why did an article like this appear?

313
00:22:45,297 --> 00:22:46,865
I'm very sorry.

314
00:22:47,132 --> 00:22:51,503
We even sent Professor Hijikata over,
but all that went for nothing.

315
00:22:54,172 --> 00:22:55,474
What's even worse,

316
00:22:56,274 --> 00:23:00,545
we're now branded
as a hospital with zero credibility.

317
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:05,917
I deeply apologize.

318
00:23:05,984 --> 00:23:08,253
Your apology won't solve anything.

319
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:10,055
This is causing us trouble, too.

320
00:23:10,122 --> 00:23:12,491
The main hospital is losing
a bunch of patients, too.

321
00:23:12,591 --> 00:23:13,625
Take responsibility.

322
00:23:14,626 --> 00:23:17,295
Do you have
any corrective measures in mind?

323
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:23,301
I will work tirelessly
to restore the hospital's credibility,

324
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:28,507
but there cannot be
any future for the current staff.

325
00:23:28,974 --> 00:23:31,510
Surgery Department II
at the Third Hospital

326
00:23:32,677 --> 00:23:35,046
will be dissolved immediately.

327
00:23:39,651 --> 00:23:42,754
Well, I guess that's all you can do.

328
00:23:44,589 --> 00:23:45,424
Yes, sir.

329
00:23:45,524 --> 00:23:51,963
Yes, sir.

330
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:54,199
Yes, sir.

331
00:23:57,969 --> 00:24:02,541
No one told me about
a freelance sinister doctor.

332
00:24:03,375 --> 00:24:08,980
She was hired urgently
to fill the shortage of surgeons. But,

333
00:24:10,182 --> 00:24:11,750
Michiko Daimon is...

334
00:24:13,185 --> 00:24:14,953
uncontrollable.

335
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:16,955
Uncontrollable?

336
00:24:18,423 --> 00:24:21,693
But actually, the outcome will be fine.

337
00:24:22,561 --> 00:24:27,132
If we take this opportunity
to overhaul the entire hospital,

338
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,635
and make it an outpost
of Teito University,

339
00:24:31,736 --> 00:24:34,873
you can completely take away
its authority over personnel matters.

340
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:40,412
Won't that make things
a lot easier for you, too?

341
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:46,284
That may be so.

342
00:25:04,936 --> 00:25:08,340
I'm back after being gone a while,
but it's deserted.

343
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:10,876
As if it's someone else's matter.

344
00:25:10,942 --> 00:25:13,411
Whose fault is it
that things turned out like this?

345
00:25:17,382 --> 00:25:20,919
You don't give a damn
what happens to the hospital.

346
00:25:20,986 --> 00:25:21,853
Right.

347
00:25:22,687 --> 00:25:25,290
But I can't have less surgeries.

348
00:25:30,128 --> 00:25:33,298
That bag. Who bought it for you?

349
00:25:33,899 --> 00:25:34,966
Why?

350
00:25:35,033 --> 00:25:36,234
SECRETARY
AI OKUMURA

351
00:25:36,301 --> 00:25:39,938
I just want to let you know
I didn't get this from Professor Torii.

352
00:25:40,005 --> 00:25:41,673
Whose present is it, then?

353
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:44,643
I'm not
the Surgery Chief secretary anymore.

354
00:25:45,076 --> 00:25:46,511
Oh, really?

355
00:25:48,313 --> 00:25:50,782
Professor Torii's wife's liver

356
00:25:50,849 --> 00:25:52,684
will be guarding him
for the rest of his life.

357
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:54,286
I'm too scared to approach him.

358
00:25:57,856 --> 00:26:00,559
I looked around and transferred
to a different department.

359
00:26:05,330 --> 00:26:08,667
Ms. Okumura's now secretary
of the anesthesiology professor.

360
00:26:11,836 --> 00:26:13,939
She already found her next prey.

361
00:26:14,706 --> 00:26:16,942
We can't afford to lose our jobs.

362
00:26:17,776 --> 00:26:21,012
Everyone is desperate. Unlike you.

363
00:26:27,652 --> 00:26:30,989
This is rather sudden,
but personnel rotation was decided

364
00:26:31,289 --> 00:26:33,158
at the main hospital professors' meeting.

365
00:26:33,391 --> 00:26:35,594
Since Professor Torii is
under medical care,

366
00:26:35,961 --> 00:26:40,031
I will give you the notice
of appointment in his place.

367
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:41,366
Dr. Kaji.

368
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:43,401
Yes.

369
00:26:44,202 --> 00:26:45,503
Starting from the new year,

370
00:26:46,004 --> 00:26:48,974
you'll be at a satellite hospital
in Takamatsu.

371
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,346
- Dr. Hara.
- Yes.

372
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:58,149
Doctor, you'll be going
to our affiliate in Asahikawa.

373
00:26:59,784 --> 00:27:00,685
I understand.

374
00:27:01,152 --> 00:27:02,754
- Dr. Morimoto.
- Yes.

375
00:27:02,821 --> 00:27:06,658
There's a shortage of assistants
at our research facility in Chiba.

376
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:12,597
Please devote yourself to assisting
the professors and their assistants.

377
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,867
That's all.

378
00:27:16,334 --> 00:27:17,435
- Manager.
- Yes?

379
00:27:18,737 --> 00:27:25,710
We are transferred
because of that ridiculous article?

380
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:29,381
It's so unfortunate.
I'm at loss for words.

381
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:35,854
However, this was decided
by the professors at the main hospital.

382
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:37,322
I agree.

383
00:27:37,389 --> 00:27:39,557
I can't go along
with a reassignment like this.

384
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:45,664
Come on, now.
This is putting me on the spot, too.

385
00:27:45,930 --> 00:27:48,133
We're already short of surgeons as it is.

386
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:51,536
What am I supposed to do
after I lose all three of you at once?

387
00:27:51,836 --> 00:27:55,640
The main hospital thinks
of satellite hospitals as outposts.

388
00:27:55,707 --> 00:27:58,209
They only think of us
as stepping stones to their own success.

389
00:27:58,276 --> 00:28:00,879
Worst comes to worst, they think
they can let the weak carry the load

390
00:28:00,945 --> 00:28:04,282
and send them packing elsewhere.
Screw them all.

391
00:28:05,083 --> 00:28:06,751
Just because
we go around saying "Yes, sir,"

392
00:28:06,818 --> 00:28:09,354
all those idiots and Busujima, too,
are getting damn arrogant.

393
00:28:09,421 --> 00:28:10,355
Yes, ma'am.

394
00:28:10,422 --> 00:28:12,157
Is it the only thing you can say?

395
00:28:12,891 --> 00:28:15,160
- Yes, ma'am.
- What are you looking at?

396
00:28:20,932 --> 00:28:23,835
Gentlemen, it's as you heard.

397
00:28:23,935 --> 00:28:26,638
Please finish transitioning by year-end
and put in your best effort

398
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:30,975
at your new hospital
when the new year begins.

399
00:28:34,512 --> 00:28:35,447
You, too.

400
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:44,522
The weather sure turned nice.

401
00:28:45,323 --> 00:28:48,093
I love these white gowns.

402
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:53,198
ASAHIKAWA, CHIBA

403
00:28:53,264 --> 00:28:54,499
Takamatsu...

404
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:57,102
Where was it again?

405
00:28:57,635 --> 00:28:58,536
As I recall,

406
00:28:59,204 --> 00:29:01,573
it's a warm place where tangerines grow.

407
00:29:02,474 --> 00:29:06,010
Asahikawa's cold.
Be careful not to catch a cold.

408
00:29:07,879 --> 00:29:11,249
I hear its lowest temperature
is -20 Celsius.

409
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:12,951
Is that right?

410
00:29:13,384 --> 00:29:16,855
- Then watch out for frostbite.
- Yes.

411
00:29:18,690 --> 00:29:19,991
What is it!

412
00:29:20,058 --> 00:29:24,062
If you get really bad frostbite
and need amputation, let me do it.

413
00:29:24,529 --> 00:29:25,697
I don't make mistakes.

414
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,799
Whose fault is it
that we're in this situation?

415
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:30,468
- Me.
- Do something about it, then.

416
00:29:31,536 --> 00:29:32,570
That's right!

417
00:29:32,637 --> 00:29:35,039
If you tell them you did
everything on your own,

418
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:37,809
- they might retract our reassignment.
- You're good at that, aren't you?

419
00:29:37,876 --> 00:29:40,445
Just march into the Director's office
and do your usual thing.

420
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:42,213
Dr. Daimon, please, I beg you.

421
00:29:43,314 --> 00:29:45,583
- Why should I?
- Why?

422
00:29:47,285 --> 00:29:49,120
Even if it was only for three months,

423
00:29:50,088 --> 00:29:52,724
we're comrades who fought together
in the operating room.

424
00:29:53,124 --> 00:29:54,392
Even someone like you

425
00:29:54,759 --> 00:29:57,228
- would certainly help friends in trouble.
- No, I won't.

426
00:29:57,295 --> 00:30:00,064
Even you would have something
like a guilty conscience.

427
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:02,333
- No, I don't.
- You don't!

428
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:05,570
It's because of your overbearing attitude
like that we got dragged into this.

429
00:30:05,637 --> 00:30:08,306
- Can't you at least reflect on--
- No, I won't.

430
00:30:10,542 --> 00:30:12,710
I don't want to go to the research center.

431
00:30:13,244 --> 00:30:15,213
Aren't you taking over
your family's clinic?

432
00:30:16,381 --> 00:30:18,049
That's what my parents say.

433
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:20,785
That it's about time for me
to take over. But I can't decide.

434
00:30:21,252 --> 00:30:23,721
Your annual income
will increase by leaps and bounds,

435
00:30:23,788 --> 00:30:25,557
and you'll be released
from night duties, too.

436
00:30:25,623 --> 00:30:29,027
But I want to be a surgeon
who can save any patient.

437
00:30:30,161 --> 00:30:31,830
Dr. Daimon, what do you think I should do?

438
00:30:31,896 --> 00:30:33,698
Come on, why the hell are you asking her?

439
00:30:36,768 --> 00:30:39,037
Why not tell them
research is something I won't do?

440
00:30:39,103 --> 00:30:41,039
That'll just get me fired!

441
00:30:41,105 --> 00:30:42,273
Then get fired.

442
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:44,242
That's cold.

443
00:30:45,176 --> 00:30:47,212
Are you okay? How could you be, huh?

444
00:30:47,278 --> 00:30:49,614
Stop rubbing us the wrong way
with everything you say.

445
00:30:50,882 --> 00:30:51,883
What a pain.

446
00:30:56,521 --> 00:31:02,193
Ms. Daimon, your contract ends today
at 5:00 p.m.

447
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,129
- And a renewal?
- Why would we do that?

448
00:31:06,164 --> 00:31:07,398
Yes, ma'am.

449
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:09,334
I'm taking lunch, then.

450
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:14,372
Damn her!

451
00:31:14,505 --> 00:31:17,375
- She's so carefree.
- You shouldn't get involved any further.

452
00:31:17,842 --> 00:31:20,678
If this article's true,
she's really dangerous.

453
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:22,146
That Demon's been

454
00:31:22,213 --> 00:31:24,749
performing dangerous surgeries,
causing a number of deaths, right?

455
00:31:25,316 --> 00:31:27,952
My goodness! Lord help us.

456
00:31:34,759 --> 00:31:37,362
I'm off to Nagoya, they said.

457
00:31:44,936 --> 00:31:47,438
I bought that condo
close to this hospital.

458
00:31:47,505 --> 00:31:49,107
On a 35-year mortgage.

459
00:31:50,108 --> 00:31:53,211
We finally got in the day care
after being on the waiting list.

460
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:56,080
Mai finally made some new friends.

461
00:31:58,616 --> 00:31:59,984
All that is going poof.

462
00:32:01,853 --> 00:32:04,856
These things that are important
to normal people,

463
00:32:05,523 --> 00:32:07,659
you don't understand at all, do you?

464
00:32:09,093 --> 00:32:10,161
No, I don't.

465
00:32:11,062 --> 00:32:14,532
To be sure, you're a good surgeon.

466
00:32:15,066 --> 00:32:18,202
But at a university hospital, there are
not-so-competent and weak doctors, too.

467
00:32:18,336 --> 00:32:22,140
We all covered for each other
and somehow managed to keep it running.

468
00:32:22,206 --> 00:32:23,474
Until you came.

469
00:32:23,541 --> 00:32:25,176
But that's not right, is it?

470
00:32:25,643 --> 00:32:27,111
But that's what an organization is.

471
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,448
Out of 100 doctors,

472
00:32:31,349 --> 00:32:32,817
you have ten good ones.

473
00:32:33,084 --> 00:32:34,852
If those ten doctors covered for the rest,

474
00:32:34,919 --> 00:32:38,356
mistakes are bound to occur,
and they'll die of exhaustion.

475
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,560
Should you help the incompetent doctors?

476
00:32:43,895 --> 00:32:45,763
Doctors are supposed to help patients.

477
00:32:46,397 --> 00:32:50,768
That's why not everyone
can live as they please like you.

478
00:32:50,835 --> 00:32:51,669
Why?

479
00:32:55,106 --> 00:32:57,041
Can you entrust your precious life...

480
00:32:57,775 --> 00:33:00,511
to a university hospital like this?

481
00:33:03,514 --> 00:33:04,983
In the operating room,

482
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:08,186
you don't need cozy ties,
or cooperation, or "Yes, sir."

483
00:33:09,854 --> 00:33:12,357
All you have is a patient
who needs to be saved.

484
00:33:17,595 --> 00:33:21,699
Not all doctors have confidence like you.

485
00:33:25,069 --> 00:33:26,904
I don't have confidence myself.

486
00:33:28,139 --> 00:33:30,041
I do have a weapon, though.

487
00:33:30,108 --> 00:33:30,942
What?

488
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:37,415
The pressure that
I can't fail is my weapon.

489
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:44,422
Dr. Jonouchi, you should be
a freelance doctor, too.

490
00:33:45,189 --> 00:33:47,225
I'll introduce you to a good manager.

491
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:51,229
His fees are a little steep,
but he'll babysit, too. How about it?

492
00:33:56,067 --> 00:33:57,635
Doctor X.

493
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:06,210
After all those things written
about you, no one's protecting you.

494
00:34:09,847 --> 00:34:11,382
I don't want to get involved anymore.

495
00:34:15,486 --> 00:34:16,587
That's too bad.

496
00:34:17,989 --> 00:34:22,627
I thought Dr. Jonouchi and I
would've made a good surgery team.

497
00:34:26,431 --> 00:34:27,398
I decline.

498
00:34:47,718 --> 00:34:49,187
Did you want to see me?

499
00:34:52,156 --> 00:34:57,095
As a result of the meeting,
we've come to the conclusion

500
00:34:57,595 --> 00:35:00,965
that responsibility for this mishap
lies with you.

501
00:35:01,699 --> 00:35:03,668
Wait... Wait a minute.

502
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:05,303
You're terminated.

503
00:35:08,306 --> 00:35:12,043
- Are you okay with that, sir?
- Yes.

504
00:35:14,011 --> 00:35:15,480
But...

505
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:18,516
- Are we done here?
- Yes.

506
00:35:22,286 --> 00:35:23,354
Get out.

507
00:35:46,177 --> 00:35:47,044
Everyone.

508
00:35:50,214 --> 00:35:52,650
I apologize for the way things turned out.

509
00:35:52,717 --> 00:35:54,585
It's not your fault, Professor.

510
00:35:54,652 --> 00:35:55,686
No...

511
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:57,989
If I hadn't fallen ill,
this wouldn't have happened.

512
00:35:58,055 --> 00:36:00,358
- Professor.
- If I had...

513
00:36:01,025 --> 00:36:05,396
If I had Hijikata operate on me
like Director Busujima wanted,

514
00:36:06,664 --> 00:36:09,133
I wouldn't have caused all of you trouble.

515
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,736
- Professor...
- Professor.

516
00:36:12,203 --> 00:36:16,274
If Hijikata had operated on you,
he would've failed and you'd be dead.

517
00:36:17,074 --> 00:36:18,009
Daimon!

518
00:36:20,077 --> 00:36:21,546
I apologize deeply.

519
00:36:23,514 --> 00:36:27,919
This Surgery Department II
was a very special team to me.

520
00:36:29,654 --> 00:36:33,624
It's a shame to dissolve it,
and it angers me.

521
00:36:35,660 --> 00:36:38,496
Please don't make it
sound like a final farewell.

522
00:36:40,298 --> 00:36:43,100
We'll be back someday
to support you again.

523
00:36:44,368 --> 00:36:45,236
Kaji.

524
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:47,605
In celebration of Professor's recovery,

525
00:36:47,672 --> 00:36:50,641
and to give our word
to reunite as Surgery Department II,

526
00:36:50,708 --> 00:36:51,809
let's have a party tonight.

527
00:36:52,677 --> 00:36:55,313
I have a good champagne
given to me by a patient.

528
00:36:57,815 --> 00:36:58,816
- Professor.
- Professor!

529
00:37:00,151 --> 00:37:05,223
We'll definitely return to work
for you again someday.

530
00:37:07,291 --> 00:37:08,459
Thank you.

531
00:37:09,961 --> 00:37:11,562
I won't be returning, though.

532
00:37:11,629 --> 00:37:14,198
Stop destroying the mood every time!

533
00:37:15,166 --> 00:37:17,568
Daimon, your contract
is up today, isn't it?

534
00:37:17,768 --> 00:37:20,104
It's your final meeting.
Let's have a drink before you go.

535
00:37:24,709 --> 00:37:26,978
- To Professor. Cheers.
- Cheers!

536
00:37:38,756 --> 00:37:41,459
My contract's over. Excuse me.

537
00:37:44,161 --> 00:37:45,496
Dr. Daimon.

538
00:37:51,035 --> 00:37:54,872
MICHIKO DAIMON

539
00:38:00,144 --> 00:38:01,612
Ms. Michiko Daimon.

540
00:38:04,448 --> 00:38:06,350
This article will be published next.

541
00:38:06,417 --> 00:38:08,019
THE TRUTH BEHIND UNIVERSITY HOSPITALS

542
00:38:09,887 --> 00:38:12,223
Wait, Ms. Daimon.
Give me a comment, please.

543
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:13,357
I don't have any.

544
00:38:13,691 --> 00:38:16,627
You're admitting that you're Doctor X,
aren't you?

545
00:38:17,261 --> 00:38:20,298
Then wasn't your medical license
revoked a long time ago?

546
00:38:20,898 --> 00:38:24,669
Did you forge a license
to sneak into the university hospital?

547
00:38:26,203 --> 00:38:28,205
Why don't you say something? Dai--

548
00:38:40,951 --> 00:38:42,253
Are you all right?

549
00:38:42,386 --> 00:38:43,954
- Emergency endoscopy!
- Yes!

550
00:38:44,021 --> 00:38:45,489
- Please bring a stretcher!
- Yes!

551
00:38:45,556 --> 00:38:47,391
- Call Gastrointestinal, stat!
- Yes!

552
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:58,869
- Professor, get well soon.
- Thank you.

553
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:02,840
White gowns and research papers
go well with you.

554
00:39:03,874 --> 00:39:05,743
Dr. Kaji. Emergency surgery, please.

555
00:39:05,810 --> 00:39:09,447
42-year-old male. Massive bleeding
from tumor or lesion in stomach.

556
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:12,283
State of shock from bleeding.
Emergency surgery is needed.

557
00:39:12,383 --> 00:39:13,451
- Kaji.
- Yes.

558
00:39:13,651 --> 00:39:14,518
First Assistant, Hara.

559
00:39:14,585 --> 00:39:16,187
- Second Assistant, Morimoto.
- Yes.

560
00:39:16,253 --> 00:39:17,455
- I'm counting on you.
- Yes.

561
00:39:24,729 --> 00:39:25,730
I'm going first!

562
00:39:40,144 --> 00:39:43,047
It doesn't look like we'll be
going back to the party today.

563
00:39:46,417 --> 00:39:48,886
Blood pressure 75 over 50. Heart rate 125.

564
00:39:48,953 --> 00:39:51,989
- Blood flow is decreasing rapidly.
- Let's hurry.

565
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,524
We will now begin...

566
00:39:54,992 --> 00:39:56,193
What's the patient's name?

567
00:39:57,328 --> 00:39:59,764
Wait! Wait a minute!

568
00:39:59,830 --> 00:40:02,266
That patient's the reporter
who wrote that article!

569
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:04,135
What?

570
00:40:04,835 --> 00:40:07,605
When I checked his bag
to contact his family...

571
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:11,375
I found pictures and manuscripts!

572
00:40:11,442 --> 00:40:15,246
Part 2 is even worse than the first!

573
00:40:17,248 --> 00:40:21,685
If that appears,
this hospital will be finished for sure.

574
00:40:25,055 --> 00:40:27,158
We don't have to do
the surgery here, do we?

575
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:31,595
Let's treat him temporarily
with transfusion and hemostatic drug

576
00:40:31,695 --> 00:40:33,531
and transport him to another hospital.

577
00:40:33,864 --> 00:40:34,698
Yes.

578
00:40:43,741 --> 00:40:47,144
- Dr. Daimon.
- Why are you back?

579
00:40:47,211 --> 00:40:50,114
No one wants to do it? Then let me do it.

580
00:40:51,582 --> 00:40:54,819
Prepare for transfusion.
Get me ten units of MAP.

581
00:40:55,820 --> 00:40:58,055
Why are you standing there?
Until the blood gets here,

582
00:40:58,122 --> 00:40:59,757
give him a full dose of volume expander.

583
00:41:00,724 --> 00:41:03,160
- Stop it.
- If you save this patient,

584
00:41:03,694 --> 00:41:05,463
he'll write half-truths again.

585
00:41:05,896 --> 00:41:06,730
So?

586
00:41:06,797 --> 00:41:09,200
He wrote the worst things
about you, Dr. Daimon.

587
00:41:10,935 --> 00:41:11,936
Doctor--

588
00:41:12,002 --> 00:41:15,206
If you hate this patient that much,
after the surgery is over,

589
00:41:15,272 --> 00:41:17,675
you can do whatever you want with him.

590
00:41:36,894 --> 00:41:37,828
Demon.

591
00:41:38,696 --> 00:41:40,231
Just for today, you can make mistakes.

592
00:41:40,297 --> 00:41:41,932
I don't make mistakes.

593
00:41:47,938 --> 00:41:49,673
- Suction, please.
- Yes.

594
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:51,742
- Bring me the blood.
- Yes.

595
00:42:15,666 --> 00:42:17,001
I can see the pylorus.

596
00:42:17,067 --> 00:42:18,302
- Metzen.
- Yes.

597
00:42:18,969 --> 00:42:21,071
We can make do with
a partial resection of the stomach.

598
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:23,340
- Forceps.
- Yes.

599
00:42:23,874 --> 00:42:25,109
- Gauze.
- Yes.

600
00:42:27,044 --> 00:42:28,112
Gauze.

601
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:30,381
Morimoto,

602
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:32,716
- open up the surgical area some more.
- Yes.

603
00:42:41,992 --> 00:42:42,826
Director.

604
00:42:50,935 --> 00:42:52,069
Who's the patient?

605
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,005
Well. Everyone tried to stop her,

606
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:57,708
but Ms. Daimon
started operating by herself.

607
00:42:57,775 --> 00:42:58,776
Look at this.

608
00:43:19,296 --> 00:43:20,197
Look.

609
00:43:28,172 --> 00:43:30,074
Blood pressure 100 over 60.

610
00:43:31,642 --> 00:43:32,977
- Auto suture.
- Yes.

611
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:43,754
Excuse me.

612
00:44:36,373 --> 00:44:37,241
Finished.

613
00:44:56,493 --> 00:44:57,361
Dr. Daimon.

614
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:06,637
Thank you for your work.

615
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:08,238
Thank you.

616
00:45:08,872 --> 00:45:10,007
Thank you.

617
00:45:12,009 --> 00:45:13,444
Thank you.

618
00:45:13,911 --> 00:45:14,978
Thank you.

619
00:45:15,813 --> 00:45:17,448
Thank you.

620
00:45:21,285 --> 00:45:22,653
Bye-bye.

621
00:46:26,183 --> 00:46:28,252
Good morning, Ben Casey.

622
00:46:30,020 --> 00:46:32,389
- Michiko, are you going somewhere?
- Yeah.

623
00:46:34,391 --> 00:46:35,726
I'm coming.

624
00:46:40,731 --> 00:46:43,734
Director Busujima, how may I help you?

625
00:46:45,669 --> 00:46:48,338
I'd like to speak with Daimon.

626
00:46:56,380 --> 00:46:57,481
Daimon.

627
00:47:01,385 --> 00:47:02,619
What now?

628
00:47:03,854 --> 00:47:06,290
As I was watching the surgery last night,

629
00:47:06,790 --> 00:47:09,159
I was reminded of an old comrade.

630
00:47:11,895 --> 00:47:13,230
It's your father.

631
00:47:17,601 --> 00:47:20,904
For him, no matter who the patient was,

632
00:47:21,605 --> 00:47:23,740
or what the other professors said,

633
00:47:24,775 --> 00:47:28,645
he would operate to save the patient.

634
00:47:30,080 --> 00:47:31,882
That's the kind of surgeon he was.

635
00:47:34,518 --> 00:47:36,820
His surgical skills were remarkable

636
00:47:37,955 --> 00:47:43,126
and I, as a fellow surgeon,
envied your father.

637
00:47:45,162 --> 00:47:46,163
Daimon.

638
00:47:47,598 --> 00:47:49,967
You took after your father, didn't you?

639
00:47:53,570 --> 00:47:54,538
Thanks.

640
00:47:55,005 --> 00:47:57,107
However, at your young age,

641
00:47:57,574 --> 00:48:00,043
to learn all those skills

642
00:48:01,211 --> 00:48:03,180
is no ordinary thing.

643
00:48:09,119 --> 00:48:15,459
You probably went through
unimaginable training.

644
00:48:18,662 --> 00:48:22,532
You must've gone through
a vast number of surgery sites...

645
00:48:24,635 --> 00:48:29,306
and made superhuman effort.

646
00:48:36,346 --> 00:48:37,547
So?

647
00:48:40,784 --> 00:48:43,687
Where is your father's grave?

648
00:48:52,629 --> 00:48:55,699
It's near Daimon Clinic,
which you destroyed.

649
00:49:01,838 --> 00:49:02,673
I see.

650
00:49:10,047 --> 00:49:12,916
Daimon. If you don't mind,

651
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:17,988
will you go visit his grave with me?

652
00:49:21,558 --> 00:49:22,492
Please.

653
00:49:33,236 --> 00:49:34,371
I'm not doing it.

654
00:49:37,074 --> 00:49:38,542
I'm in a bit of a rush.

655
00:49:41,378 --> 00:49:44,147
- Where are you going in such a rush?
- I'm going.

656
00:49:50,287 --> 00:49:51,955
I'm very sorry.

657
00:49:53,023 --> 00:49:57,761
If she can only learn her manners,

658
00:49:57,828 --> 00:50:00,630
she can be a formidable surgeon.

659
00:50:01,264 --> 00:50:05,268
Anyway, if you're so inclined,
please hire her again.

660
00:50:06,169 --> 00:50:09,306
Actually, I've become unemployed.

661
00:50:10,707 --> 00:50:13,076
I will leave the hospital soon.

662
00:50:13,143 --> 00:50:15,979
Oh, my. That's tough luck.

663
00:50:16,046 --> 00:50:20,317
Excuse me for bringing it up
at a time like this, but here.

664
00:50:22,019 --> 00:50:25,155
The bill for last night's
emergency surgery.

665
00:50:25,222 --> 00:50:26,656
600,000 YEN

666
00:50:29,426 --> 00:50:31,094
I haven't made you tea.

667
00:50:31,528 --> 00:50:34,164
Just a minute.
Would you like your melon now?

668
00:50:34,765 --> 00:50:38,468
No, thanks. Your melons
always end up costing me.

669
00:50:40,504 --> 00:50:42,005
Excuse me for intruding.

670
00:50:53,617 --> 00:50:55,652
GRACIAS
MICHIKO

671
00:51:05,862 --> 00:51:07,064
What?

672
00:51:08,365 --> 00:51:09,466
It can't be.

673
00:51:10,467 --> 00:51:12,469
The real Doctor X is...

674
00:51:18,308 --> 00:51:20,944
I'll be coming over to collect,

675
00:51:21,511 --> 00:51:23,513
so I'll be looking forward
to seeing you later.

676
00:51:26,483 --> 00:51:27,951
I will bring a melon to you.

677
00:51:32,322 --> 00:51:34,724
<i>"There are doctors who undauntedly</i>
<i>rise to the challenge</i>

678
00:51:35,325 --> 00:51:39,429
<i>of performing dangerous surgeries</i>
<i>with low success and survival rate</i>

679
00:51:39,496 --> 00:51:42,132
surgeries with yet established
surgical procedures.

680
00:51:42,199 --> 00:51:45,802
With respect and sarcasm,
these doctors are called,

681
00:51:47,170 --> 00:51:50,140
evil doctors who place
human lives on a scale.

682
00:51:50,807 --> 00:51:53,844
Also known as 'Doctor X.'"

683
00:51:55,846 --> 00:51:59,116
So, there's more than one
Doctor X all over the world.

684
00:52:00,750 --> 00:52:03,487
<i>"However, they're not just reckless.</i>

685
00:52:03,987 --> 00:52:05,922
<i>It's also true that</i>
<i>with their outstanding skills,</i>

686
00:52:05,989 --> 00:52:09,059
<i>they developed surgical procedures</i>
<i>the medical world shied away from,</i>

687
00:52:09,659 --> 00:52:12,796
<i>and saved lives that otherwise</i>
<i>would have been lost."</i>

688
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:18,768
Doctor X, huh?
That's just an absurd rumor.

689
00:52:18,835 --> 00:52:23,273
But we may soon be needing

690
00:52:24,407 --> 00:52:28,578
people like that at university hospitals.

691
00:52:29,479 --> 00:52:30,780
Professor Teshigawara!

692
00:52:34,184 --> 00:52:35,519
Chief Director's calling for you.

693
00:52:49,633 --> 00:52:50,667
Excuse me.

694
00:52:54,638 --> 00:52:58,875
Well, doctors.
You've had it tough recently.

695
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:02,812
Re-employment for doctors
with a past is difficult.

696
00:53:02,879 --> 00:53:04,848
Please come see me anytime.

697
00:53:04,915 --> 00:53:07,584
I'll give you a discount
on management fee.

698
00:53:16,259 --> 00:53:17,928
I won't quit the hospital.

699
00:53:18,762 --> 00:53:20,597
Wads of money are laying around

700
00:53:20,830 --> 00:53:22,799
in the university hospital's
operating room.

701
00:53:23,200 --> 00:53:24,668
Well, excuse me.

702
00:53:25,368 --> 00:53:29,306
I'm going to strive
for a warm medical care

703
00:53:29,372 --> 00:53:31,241
with compassion
for the patients at Asahikawa.

704
00:53:31,708 --> 00:53:32,642
I see.

705
00:53:34,511 --> 00:53:36,646
I turned in my resignation today,

706
00:53:36,713 --> 00:53:39,416
so I'm a freelancer now.
I'm looking forward to working with you.

707
00:53:40,050 --> 00:53:41,117
What?

708
00:53:42,152 --> 00:53:42,986
What?

709
00:53:44,754 --> 00:53:49,192
- You babysit, too, don't you?
- I play sharks, too.

710
00:53:51,127 --> 00:53:53,096
What about you, Dr. Morimoto?

711
00:53:53,897 --> 00:53:56,967
I made up my mind.
I'm not taking over my family's clinic.

712
00:53:57,033 --> 00:54:00,203
I'm studying abroad, and striving
to be a surgeon like Dr. Daimon.

713
00:54:00,270 --> 00:54:02,572
Why Demon, and not me?

714
00:54:02,639 --> 00:54:04,307
Because she's cool.

715
00:54:04,674 --> 00:54:07,510
What's that supposed to mean?
What's that about?

716
00:54:12,749 --> 00:54:14,084
Coming through.

717
00:54:14,150 --> 00:54:16,820
<i>University hospital</i>
<i>medical offices were losing power,</i>

718
00:54:17,754 --> 00:54:19,556
<i>and even medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with life and death,</i>

719
00:54:19,623 --> 00:54:22,759
<i>plunged into an era</i>
<i>where the law of the jungle prevailed.</i>

720
00:54:34,571 --> 00:54:37,874
Professor Teshigawara.
What can I do for you?

721
00:54:40,910 --> 00:54:45,949
Because of you, I was withdrawn
from the Director's race.

722
00:54:46,750 --> 00:54:48,251
- Pardon me?
- I was...

723
00:54:49,452 --> 00:54:51,688
the leading candidate.

724
00:54:58,328 --> 00:55:00,263
What's so funny?

725
00:55:03,233 --> 00:55:04,501
It's your damn fault!

726
00:55:06,136 --> 00:55:07,737
What are you doing?

727
00:55:09,105 --> 00:55:11,808
It's your fault, damn it!

728
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:17,213
Grow up!

729
00:55:20,183 --> 00:55:21,351
Busujima!

730
00:55:24,521 --> 00:55:28,658
<i>To fill the critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field are the freelance.</i>

731
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:32,862
<i>In other words, a lone wolf doctor.</i>

732
00:55:39,035 --> 00:55:41,271
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

733
00:55:42,405 --> 00:55:44,841
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority...</i>

734
00:55:44,908 --> 00:55:45,809
MAH-JONG WINNING STRATEGIES

735
00:55:45,909 --> 00:55:47,644
<i>...and she hates constraints.</i>

736
00:55:48,712 --> 00:55:52,849
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

737
00:55:57,320 --> 00:55:59,422
Dr. Daimon, you're wanted on the phone.

738
00:55:59,656 --> 00:56:00,623
Thanks.

739
00:56:02,125 --> 00:56:02,992
Hello?

740
00:56:03,093 --> 00:56:05,962
<i>Hello, Michiko? Training abroad again?</i>

741
00:56:06,363 --> 00:56:09,432
What are you going to do,
honing up your skill all the time?

742
00:56:09,999 --> 00:56:13,069
You still have a ton of debt.
Hurry on home.

743
00:56:13,136 --> 00:56:15,839
I think I paid back quite a bit already.

744
00:56:16,106 --> 00:56:18,775
Mr. Akira, aren't you taking too much?

745
00:56:18,842 --> 00:56:20,744
Definitely not.

746
00:56:21,244 --> 00:56:25,648
Post-stomach cancer surgery
acute abdomen in Room 302.

747
00:56:26,449 --> 00:56:27,350
What?

748
00:56:27,417 --> 00:56:30,220
<i>Signs of muscular defense.</i>
<i>Get yourself there quickly.</i>

749
00:56:30,920 --> 00:56:33,456
He's a multi-millionaire
who made his money off shale gas.

750
00:56:33,790 --> 00:56:37,427
You may be able to pay off
all your debt if you save him.

751
00:56:39,863 --> 00:56:40,864
Thanks!

752
00:56:47,103 --> 00:56:48,671
- Stop.
- It's all right. She's a doctor.

753
00:56:56,479 --> 00:56:58,014
How long has he been in pain?

754
00:56:58,181 --> 00:57:00,116
He began to suffer a moment ago.

755
00:57:00,450 --> 00:57:01,751
It's ileus, most likely.

756
00:57:02,519 --> 00:57:04,087
He needs immediate surgery.

757
00:57:05,054 --> 00:57:08,091
Who's this woman exposing her legs?

758
00:57:08,158 --> 00:57:12,328
Are you sure this woman can save me?

759
00:57:13,062 --> 00:57:14,964
I don't make mistakes.

760
00:57:19,702 --> 00:57:22,238
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

761
